			},
			"date": "2024-12-30T15:55:59.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <br>Recommend you get yourself into 3D drawing apps. Can be super expensive but you don't need those - I'm using <a href=\"https://www.tinkercad.com\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://www.</span><span class=\"\">tinkercad.com</span><span class=\"invisible\"></span></a>  - free. Basic shapes and you can join them together to make more sophisticated shapes.  <br>here is a small locomotive i'm playing around with for my modelling. My printer is resin not filament though - different process.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
