			},
			"date": "2024-12-31T15:33:44.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> subscribed with interest - I've done a few prints at Do Space but struggled to find things that are useful, expensive/impractical to purchase, and don't immediately fall apart.</p><p>Probably the print that's used most is a magnetic key holder <a href=\"https://www.thingiverse.com/thing:2567267\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://www.</span><span class=\"\">thingiverse.com/thing:2567267</span><span class=\"invisible\"></span></a></p><p>I'd love to print more replacement parts, like this broken component on my Rock Band kit; but I'm not convinced that ABS is gonna hold up to an evening of drumming <a href=\"https://www.thingiverse.com/thing:5226080\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://www.</span><span class=\"\">thingiverse.com/thing:5226080</span><span class=\"invisible\"></span></a></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
